0.043 0.082 0.122 rg
56. 783.8899999999999864 Td
(Constitution of the Republic of South Africa, 1996) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 747.8899999999999864 Td
(PREAMBLE) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 726.8899999999999864 Td
(We, the people of South Africa, recognise the injustices of our past; honour those who suffered for) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 711.8899999999999864 Td
(justice and freedom in our land; respect those who have worked to build and develop our country;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 696.8899999999999864 Td
(and believe that South Africa belongs to all who live in it, united in our diversity.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 675.8899999999999864 Td
(We therefore, through our freely elected representatives, adopt this Constitution as the supreme law) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 660.8899999999999864 Td
(of the Republic so as to—) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 639.8899999999999864 Td
(• Heal the divisions of the past and establish a society based on democratic values, social justice) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 624.8899999999999864 Td
(and fundamental human rights;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 603.8899999999999864 Td
(• Lay the foundations for a democratic and open society in which government is based on the will of) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 588.8899999999999864 Td
(the people and every citizen is equally protected by law;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 567.8899999999999864 Td
(• Improve the quality of life of all citizens and free the potential of each person; and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 546.8899999999999864 Td
(• Build a united and democratic South Africa able to take its rightful place as a sovereign state in the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 531.8899999999999864 Td
(family of nations.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 510.8899999999999864 Td
(CHAPTER 1 — FOUNDING PROVISIONS) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 489.8899999999999864 Td
(1. Republic of South Africa) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 468.8899999999999864 Td
(The Republic of South Africa is one, sovereign, democratic state founded on the following values:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 447.8899999999999864 Td
(\(a\) Human dignity, the achievement of equality and the advancement of human rights and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 432.8899999999999864 Td
(freedoms.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 411.8899999999999864 Td
(\(b\) Non-racialism and non-sexism.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 390.8899999999999864 Td
(\(c\) Supremacy of the constitution and the rule of law.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 369.8899999999999864 Td
(\(d\) Universal adult suffrage, a national common voters roll, regular elections and a multi-party) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 354.8899999999999864 Td
(system of democratic government, to ensure accountability, responsiveness and openness.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 333.8899999999999864 Td
(2. Supremacy of Constitution) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 312.8899999999999864 Td
(This Constitution is the supreme law of the Republic; law or conduct inconsistent with it is invalid,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 297.8899999999999864 Td
(and the obligations imposed by it must be fulfilled.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 276.8899999999999864 Td
(CHAPTER 2 — BILL OF RIGHTS \(selected\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 255.8899999999999864 Td
(7. Rights) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 234.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) This Bill of Rights is a cornerstone of democracy in South Africa. It enshrines the rights of all) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 219.8899999999999864 Td
(people in our country and affirms the democratic values of human dignity, equality and freedom.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 198.8899999999999864 Td
(9. Equality) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 177.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) Everyone is equal before the law and has the right to equal protection and benefit of the law.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 156.8899999999999864 Td
(\(3\) The state may not unfairly discriminate directly or indirectly against anyone on one or more) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 141.8899999999999864 Td
(grounds, including race, gender, sex, pregnancy, marital status, ethnic or social origin, colour,) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 126.8899999999999864 Td
(sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, conscience, belief, culture, language and birth.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 105.8899999999999864 Td
(10. Human dignity) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.114 0.18 0.251 rg
56. 84.8899999999999864 Td
(Everyone has inherent dignity and the right to have their dignity respected and protected.) Tj
ET
