(12. Freedom and security of the person) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 762.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) Everyone has the right to freedom and security of the person, which includes the right—) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 741.8899999999999864 Td
(\(a\) not to be deprived of freedom arbitrarily or without just cause;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 720.8899999999999864 Td
(\(b\) not to be detained without trial;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 699.8899999999999864 Td
(\(c\) to be free from all forms of violence from either public or private sources;) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 678.8899999999999864 Td
(\(d\) not to be tortured in any way; and) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 657.8899999999999864 Td
(\(e\) not to be treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 636.8899999999999864 Td
(25. Property) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 615.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) No one may be deprived of property except in terms of law of general application, and no law may permit arbitrary deprivation of) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 600.8899999999999864 Td
(property.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 579.8899999999999864 Td
(26. Housing) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 558.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) Everyone has the right to have access to adequate housing.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 537.8899999999999864 Td
(\(2\) The state must take reasonable legislative and other measures, within its available resources, to achieve the progressive realisation) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 522.8899999999999864 Td
(of this right.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 501.8899999999999864 Td
(\(3\) No one may be evicted from their home, or have their home demolished, without an order of court made after considering all the) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 486.8899999999999864 Td
(relevant circumstances. No legislation may permit arbitrary evictions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 465.8899999999999864 Td
(33. Just administrative action) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 444.8899999999999864 Td
(\(1\) Everyone has the right to administrative action that is lawful, reasonable and procedurally fair.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 423.8899999999999864 Td
(34. Access to courts) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 402.8899999999999864 Td
(Everyone has the right to have any dispute that can be resolved by the application of law decided in a fair public hearing before a court) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 387.8899999999999864 Td
(or, where appropriate, another independent and impartial tribunal or forum.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 366.8899999999999864 Td
(36. Limitation of rights) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.392 g
56. 345.8899999999999864 Td
